    "q-42557": {
      "dom_id": "step-q42557",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "In a particular city, about $60%$ of mornings are cloudy and $30%$ of days are rainy. \nIt is known that $40%$ of rainy days start with cloudy mornings. What is the probability that a randomly selected cloudy morning continues as a rainy day?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $C$ be the event that a randomly selected morning is cloudy, and let $R$ be the event that a randomly selected day is rainy. Then, we require $P(R|C),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(R|C)=\\frac{P(C|R)P(R)}{P(C)}\n$$\n\n- $P(C)=0.6,$ since $60%$ of mornings are cloudy.\n\n- $P(R)=0.3,$ since $30%$ of days are rainy.\n\n- $P(C|R)=0.4,$ since $40%$ of rainy days start with cloudy mornings.\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(R|C) & =\\frac{P(C|R)P(R)}{P(C)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.4\\cdot 0.3}{0.6} \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
