    "q-42569": {
      "dom_id": "step-q42569",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "On a particular industrial estate, the probability of smoke on a given day is $10%$ and the probability of a dangerous fire is $1.5%.$ It is known that $90%$ of dangerous fires create smoke. What is the probability of a dangerous fire when there is smoke? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $S$ be the event that there is smoke, and let $F$ be the event that there is a dangerous fire. Then, we require $P(F|S),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(F|S)=\\frac{P(S|F)P(F)}{P(S)}\n$$\n\n- $P(S)=0.1,$ since the probability of smoke is $10%.$\n\n- $P(F)=0.015,$ since the probability of dangerous fire is $1.5%.$\n\n- $P(S|F)=0.9,$ since  $90%$ of dangerous fires make smoke.\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F|S) & =\\frac{P(S|F)P(F)}{P(S)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.9\\cdot 0.015}{0.1} \\\\  & ≈0.14,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
