    "q-106224": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106224",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "A survey of Bulgarian citizens showed that $17%$ of all females and  $38%$ of all males smoke. $51%$ of the population are female. If a smoker from this population is selected at random, what is the probability of them being female? Express your answer as a percentage to the nearest percent.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $S$ be the event that a randomly selected person smokes, and let $F$ be the event that they are female. Then, we require $P(F|S),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(F|S)=\\frac{P(S|F)P(F)}{P(S)}=\\frac{P(S|F)P(F)}{P(S|F)P(F)+P(S|{F}^{′})P({F}^{′})}\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have the following:\n\n- Since $17%$ of all females and  $38%$ of all males smoke, we have\n\n$$\nP(S|F)=0.17,\\,P(S|{F}^{′})=0.38.\n$$\n\n- Since $51%$ of the population are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=0.51,\\,P({F}^{′})=1-0.51=0.49.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F|S) & =\\frac{P(S|F)P(F)}{P(S|F)P(F)+P(S|{F}^{′})P({F}^{′})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.17)(0.51)}{(0.17)(0.51)+(0.38)(0.49)} \\\\  & ≈32%\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest percent.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
